.TH SCAN_PB_TYPE0_SINT 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
scan_pb_type0_sint \- Scan a Protocol Buffers signed integer type 0 from a string

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/scan.h>

.IB size_t
.IB scan_pb_type0_sint(const char* in, size_t len, int64* l);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBscan_pb_type0_sint\fR function scans a Protocol Buffers signed integer type 0 from a given string and stores the result.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB in
The input string containing the Protocol Buffers signed integer type 0.
.TP
.IB len
The length of the input string.
.TP
.IB l
The destination where the scanned signed integer will be stored.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters processed.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBscan_pb_type0_sint\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/scan.h>

int main() {
    const char* sint = "\x0a";
    int64 result;
    size_t length = scan_pb_type0_sint(sint, 1, &result);
    printf("Scanned signed integer: %lld\n", result);
    printf("Length processed: %zu\n", length);
    return 0;
}
.nef